{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_kZHm2urXUHDSLbKhcRbgAqhO","content":"1\t# Python snapshot evaluation\n2\t\n3\tDraft r1, 2026-11-27 · awaiting plan review and owner decisions · auto=false. The owner requested planning. No panel was selected or run. Completion requires the phase results below and a separate milestone-close ruling.\n4\t\n5\t## 0. Binding design rules\n6\t\n7\tPreserve redaction and per-target limits across envelopes, including malformed input. A failure before evaluation must never look like an empty successful check. Use existing loaders, ModelIndex for model queries and the defining component for policy. State validation order at each public boundary and test both sides of every refusal.\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Scope, sources and authority\n10\t\n11\tIssue requirements come from [#326](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/326), [#328](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/328), [#329](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/329), [#331](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/331), [#333](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/333), including their proposed changes and reproduction examples. Implementation baseline 83cd4170. The [predecessor close](../../incremental-evaluation/012-milestone-close.md) records the inherited capability and the limits of its evidence. These are framework features; a domain experiment census cannot establish API or evaluator behavior.\n12\t\n13\t## 2. Proposed behavior\n14\t\n15\tNormalize the supported snapshot envelopes and expose the CLI vacuity acceptance option to Python. Document inventory-grounded participation with empty and missing coverage.\n16\t\n17\tReturn requested derived rows, availability and findings from a single evaluation, with disclosure and size limits. Distinguish a complete empty extension from one that could not be computed.\n18\t\n19\tReuse loaded snapshot indexes across ordered why-not targets. Replay a fully grounded negative premise only with covered relations. Report per-target work and exhaustion.\n20\t\n21\tTest shared dependency ranges against pinned builds and an independent host. Specify and exercise a versioned persistent local worker with repeated requests, structured errors and model invalidation.\n22\t\n23\t## 3. Dependencies and artifact homes\n24\t\n25\tPS2 and PS3 consume PS1 statuses. PS4 may measure dependency compatibility independently; the worker protocol freezes after the result and explanation contracts. Start with [src/gnd/api.py](../../../../src/gnd/api.py). The component index identifies `cli.api`, `check.service`, `checker.reports`, `witness.service`. Its November 27 review flagged 105 descriptions older than their source; resolve contract details against code and tests.\n26\t\n27\t## 4. Obligations and completion criteria\n28\t\n29\t| Phase | Issue and deliverable | Observable exit criterion |\n30\t|---|---|---|\n31\t| PS1 | [#333](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/333) [#331](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/331) Interpret snapshot reports | Normalize the supported snapshot envelopes and expose the CLI vacuity acceptance option to Python. Document inventory-grounded participation with empty and missing coverage. |\n32\t| PS2 | [#326](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/326) Return computed extensions | Return requested derived rows, availability and findings from a single evaluation, with disclosure and size limits. Distinguish a complete empty extension from one that could not be computed. |\n33\t| PS3 | [#328](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/328) Explain a batch | Reuse loaded snapshot indexes across ordered why-not targets. Replay a fully grounded negative premise only with covered relations. Report per-target work and exhaustion. |\n34\t| PS4 | [#329](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/329) Embed or isolate the evaluator | Test shared dependency ranges against pinned builds and an independent host. Specify and exercise a versioned persistent local worker with repeated requests, structured errors and model invalidation. |\n35\t\n36\tThe [first draft spec](phase-PS1-spec.md) expands PS1. Later specs follow the preceding decisions. Carry the predecessor’s documented limits into each new public claim.\n37\t\n38\t## 5. Documentation and compatibility\n39\t\n40\tPS1 owns the Python API reference and paired CLI example. PS2 and PS3 own disclosure tests and PS4 owns installation and worker lifecycle documentation. Start from [docs/reference/python-api.md](../../../../docs/reference/python-api.md). Run existing examples and compare the observable result for a caller using the previous interface.\n41\t\n42\t## 6. Risks and controls\n43\t\n44\tPreserve redaction and per-target limits across envelopes, including malformed input. A failure before evaluation must never look like an empty successful check. Vary identifiers, declaration order and input cardinality in the acceptance fixtures. Record work counters and the first refusal where limits apply.\n45\t\n46\t## 7. Outside this milestone\n47\t\n48\tHosted network service and broad dependency upgrades. Release scheduling belongs to the owner.\n49\t\n50\t## 8. Execution and review\n51\t\n52\tEach phase needs its own spec and owner ruling, implementation, focused tests, independent diff review, refactoring review and numbered record. Plan and close require the project’s four-reviewer bar, recorded against the reviewed bytes. The owner selects the panel. Merge and release have separate authority.\n53\t\n54\t## 9. Verification and baseline\n55\t\n56\tObserved at intake: The issue fixtures exercise raw schemas 7, 12 and 14. A missing population exits 3 with zero failed constraints. A two-target why-not request is refused. The dependency metadata pins Pydantic 2.13.4.\n57\t\n58\tRun the first spec’s focused selection and retain its verbatim pytest summary. For each later phase, use the issue reproduction and the criterion in §4 as an acceptance pair, pin the old behavior on unextended inputs and record the public entry point and result. Milestone closure requires a replay across phases, a disposition for each issue and an inventory of unverified claims. Native backend claims require native execution.\n59\t\n60\tPS2: compare requested inferred rows to a hand-built extension from the #326 fixture; count evaluations, expecting one. Exercise a redacted role and a capped extension. PS3: replay two targets against one loaded snapshot and invalidate a negative witness when the blocked relation changes. PS4: execute two requests in one isolated process, force one invalid input, then evaluate a valid request; log request IDs, model identities and restart behavior. Lockfile reproducibility and shared-host installation are separate gates.\n61\t\n62\t## 10. Open decisions\n63\t\n64\tApprove the accessor name, response fields and unsupported-schema status. Decide the supported worker transport and dependency test matrix before PS4. These are proposals for the owner. Resolve the first-phase decision before implementation; later choices may remain open through earlier phases.\n65\t\n66\t## Delegated revision 2 after six independent reviews, 2026-11-28\n67\t\n68\tThe r1 draft above preserves the reviewed text. These ruled criteria take precedence.\n69\t\n70\t1. PS1 supplies api.snapshot_verdict(report) over current plain snapshot wires 7, 9, 10, 11, 13, 15–17 and reference wrappers 12/14. Enumerate legal inner versions from the reference schema. Unknown and malformed reports have separate statuses and empty findings. A pre-evaluation or outer input failure wins over inner counts. Preserve individual constraint and derivation verdicts, warning and diagnostic records, including vacuity after an accepted opt-in run. Treat the report as supplied evidence under its original disclosure context. Protect customer-mode callers from previously unredacted input. Preserve the raw API by default. Test the real plain and both wrapped examples, missing file, conflicting outer failure, unknown version, malformed fields, and sensitive malformed inputs. Grounded inventory versus outcome coverage must exercise empty and missing relations. Verify CLI versus Python vacuity, strict boolean and incompatible options. Public component homes are api and checking_service.\n71\t2. PS2 instruments the actual checker evaluation and extension preparation, testing a rule and an equivalent renamed, reordered model plus a hand-built expected set. Return rows only when computed with full dependency coverage. Complete empty, unavailable, protected and output-limit are distinct. A relation that exceeds the row cap returns no partial rows. Cap requested relations and total returned rows; specify numerical bounds in PS2 and test equality and one extra. Compute projected disclosure before data-dependent cap reporting for a protected role. Include malformed inputs and two requested relations in the tests. Use the extension calculator in its existing check scope.\n72\t3. PS3 counts shared preparation per batch and compares ordered and reversed targets with independent singletons. Per-target counters reset; exhaust the first of two and complete the second. Ground every shared variable in a negative atom from a positive binding, require its named relation covered and prove the correlated tuple absent. Keep uncovered and exhausted distinct. Mutate the blocked relation and require a fresh evaluation to change the outcome and replay to reject stale evidence. Bound target count and per-target work at intake. The witness and replay service owns its proof format.\n73\t4. PS4 uses versioned local JSON Lines over stdio, request IDs, bounded requests, structured protocol and input failures, and a process-local session. Invalid and unsupported requests leave the worker usable. Replace model bytes at the same path, compare with a fresh session, kill and restart the worker, and prove isolation across requests. Test repository lock and independent host resolving Pydantic 2.12.x alongside the built wheel. Record tested concrete versions, narrow supported ranges to evidence, keep lock exact. Both environment tests are PS4 exit gates. This milestone makes no external database or native backend parity claim.\n74\t5. Each phase pins its own numerical limits, compatibility controls and fixture before implementation. A change to a previously approved contract requires an amendment and review-scope disclosure. The integrated close replays a supported check through accessor and worker, with single-evaluation rows and ordered explanations checked independently. Implementation evidence decides whether each requirement has been met."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_jXRqhliqtMnJKLUzHfRFNwlM","content":"1\t# Snapshot evaluation boundaries\n2\t\n3\tThe Python verdict accessor interprets supported snapshot envelopes. Public customer output stays projected. Computed rows require adequate coverage and disclosure eligibility. Why-not explains evaluator results, while certificate production and replay prove a narrower fragment. Missing coverage prevents a grounded absence proof. The worker is local, accepts standalone models, and has one cached model/session per process. Arbitrary includes and reference population dependencies are outside this protocol. Compatibility was exercised with the same wheel in two concrete Pydantic environments. Other releases inside the declared interval have not individually been run. The repository lock keeps its exact runtime resolution. No hosted deployment, database parity or release is claimed.\n4\t\n5\tAll five linked issues remain open pending merge to the default branch. Publication and release are separate owner decisions."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_3vFBsPpd6ALO9HoLSBwk7oQx","content":"1\t# Snapshot evaluation results\n2\t\n3\tThe PR implements #331 and #333 in PS1, #326 in PS2, #328 in PS3, and #329 in PS4. The numbered phase records identify the reviewed commits, covered inputs, test results and corrections.\n4\t\n5\t* PS1 exposes api.snapshot_verdict for the supported snapshot wire versions and api.check(..., allow_vacuous=True) for ordinary non-strict checks. A pre-evaluation failure retains precedence over zero failed constraints. The paired CLI and Python examples distinguish coverage, vacuous constraints and real participation. The final focused run passed 119 tests.\n6\t* PS2 observes the computed extension during the same ordinary check. It distinguishes a complete empty relation from unavailable, protected and output-limited results. Multi-clause redaction follows all dependency clauses. The broad run passed 937 tests with two deselected. Post-repair checks included 107 focused tests and 27 redaction tests.\n7\t* PS3 prepares a loaded snapshot once for an ordered batch, resets walk budgets per target and independently verifies a certificate for a covered, fully grounded asserted negative premise. Changing the blocked relation invalidates the certificate. The final affected run passed 316 checks.\n8\t* PS4 executes repeated version-1 checks in a local subprocess. The lifecycle suite checks rejection, reuse, replacement and cold restart after termination. Both separately installed hosts ran the wheel using isolated Python. The independent host used Pydantic 2.12.5 and the locked host used 2.13.4. The broad phase guard passed 912 tests with two deselected.\n9\t\n10\tThe integrated fixture in evidence/PS4/integrated_replay.py exercises all four phases in each installed host. The model fingerprint is 72c523d8e6d96f97eb0ed9cff8db70c725f2376da35dbaa525f6ab7d18aa5746. Of two candidate values, only x belongs to the requested extension. The loaded batch reports derived then blocked. A separately replayed certificate succeeds for x. Repeated worker checks surrounding an unsupported-version request have request IDs first, bad and again. The last check reuses the model. Its snapshot verdict equals the ordinary check verdict. The status is unchecked because the fixture supplies no derived claim. Both transcripts are retained alongside the script.\n11\t\n12\tThe final wheel SHA-256 is fd6c342ef66fd5ad79c42bd5f81738b82cae0488a1425809ccb7e22b73aee46e. Both hosts also evaluated an incorrect and a correct derived claim (exit 1 then 0), replaced model bytes at the same path, killed the subprocess and verified that a newly started worker cold-loaded the replacement digest."}
